== 7. Draft legend =============================================

Supplementary Figure 3. Robustness and positional specificity of the
RASSF9 promoter methylation-expression association in TCGA-SKCM.
(A) Spearman correlation between methylation beta and RASSF9 expression
for each of the seven probes in the promoter window, plotted against
strand-aware distance to the transcription start site. RASSF9 lies on the
minus strand of chromosome 12, so negative values are upstream. The five
TSS-proximal probes that constitute the promoter core correlate
negatively, whereas the two upstream shore probes correlate positively,
the island-shore inversion. (B) Regression coefficient for mean
promoter-region methylation under successive adjustment: M0 unadjusted;
M1 plus sample type; M2 plus global methylation; M3 plus global
methylation and sample type; M4 plus tumour purity. Points are point
estimates, bars 95% confidence intervals, and n is given for each model;
purity estimates are available for a subset, hence the smaller n for M4.
The coefficient does not attenuate under adjustment (-1.352 at M0 to -1.826 at M4).
(C) Each probe at the locus placed against an empirical null built from
1729 probes outside the RASSF9 and RASSF10 loci; the dashed line marks
the fifth percentile. All five promoter-core probes fall in the extreme
lower tail (below the 0.8 percentile), the distal probes lie within the
body of the null, and the two shore probes sit near the 91 percentile
in the opposite tail. Correlations are two-sided Spearman; n = 469 tumours
with paired RNA-seq and HM450 methylation.

  NOTE: the figure is drawn at 180 mm, the final printed width, so
  the smallest type is 5.5 pt as printed. Do not rescale it on the slide;
  place it at 100%.
